  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+z=2 \\\\  & 3y+2z=-1 \\\\  & -z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=2\\,\u27f9\\,z=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3y+2(-2)=-1\\,\u27f9\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(-1+4)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-2$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-2)=2\\,\u27f9\\,x=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=1$, and $z=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
